  "plain": "Apollo 11, the first crewed Moon landing mission, was launched on July 16, 1969, which Michels points out was exactly 24 years after the Trinity test, the first atomic bomb explosion and, in his words, \"the dawn of the nuclear age.\" Michels tells this himself, without naming a source, as part of an episode on NASA, ritual and secret science, where he suggests the date may have been chosen on purpose rather than by chance."
